1.create user d2 identified by sit;
(user d2 is created with password sit)
(d2 user need some permissions for database operations)

2. grant connect, resource to d2;
(permissions granted)

3. alter user d2 identified by *****;
(password can have only 0-9,a-z,A-Z only, no special characters are allowed)

4. enter username as: D2@d2
(user is now connecting to database d2)

5. commit; or exit
(exits cmd and saves all changes)



DDL
create: To create table, procedury
Table:-(st.info)
	Create table st.info(PRN int, Name varchar(20),M1 number, M2 number, 	M3 number);
3. Alter: modify the structure of the table
	Alter table st.info add Total number;
	Alter table st.info add percentage number;
	
4. Truncate: To delete all the data but not table
	Truncate table st.info;

5. Drop: Table will be deleted
	Drop table st.info;

6. Rename: Rename tables, columns in DBMS
	Alter table st.info Rename to st.information;
	Alter table st.information Rename M1 to Phy;
	Alter table st.information Rename M2 to Chem;
	Alter table st.information Rename M3 to Maths;

7. To see attributes in the table
	desc st.info

DDL language auto commits so changes are saved even without using commit and exit command.



DML
Insert command: Data into table  (Characters are inserted as string in'')
	Insert in st.info values(101, 'xyz', 55, 55, 55,null,null);
				OR
	Insert in st.info(101,'xyz',55,55,55)values(PRN,variable,M1,M2,M3);

2. Update: Update the columns
	update st.info set total=M1+M2+M3;
	update st.info set percentage=total/3;
			OR
	update st.info set total=M1+M2+M3, percentage=total/3;


